        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 10,
        "titulo": "The verb in second position, questions and negation",
        "explicacao": "The conjugated verb always stays in 2nd position. If the sentence begins with another element (today, tomorrow), the subject goes after the verb: «Heute arbeite ich.» In yes/no questions, the verb comes in 1st place: «Wohnst du in Berlin?» In questions with a question word, the word comes first and the verb second: «Wo wohnst du?» The negation «nicht» goes after the verb («Ich arbeite nicht») or before what is being negated («Ich wohne nicht in Berlin»). To say that you like doing something, use «gern» after the verb: «Ich lerne gern Deutsch».",
